<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 100,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 100,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's official Holding Company for Rice and Flour Mills said on Monday it bought a total 100,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red wheat at $189.89 and $190.75 per tonne.</p>
<p>Company chairman Kamal Ghoneim said they bought the wheat in two shipments:</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes from Continental at $189.89 per tonne for delivery between 20 and 30 September.</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes from Amiga grain at $190.75 per tonne for delivery between 20 and 30 November.</p>
<p>All prices are C+F. --Miral Fahmy +202 578 3290/91</p>
